## 1.1 Platform Analysis

✅ **Linux Deployment Feasible**

This MCP server is written in **Python** and performs OSINT tasks using common network reconnaissance tools (WHOIS, Nmap, dnsrecon, dnstwist, dig, host). All these tools are available on Linux platforms, so this server **can be deployed on Linux**.

## 1.2 Deployment Options from README

| Option | Type | Status |
|--------|------|--------|
| Smithery installation (`npx -y @smithery/cli install mcp-osint --client claude`) | Free-installation | ❌ [PROHIBITED] |

## 1.3 Custom Local Deployment Plan

Since the only documented deployment option (Smithery) is prohibited, I will design a **local deployment plan** based on the standard MCP server deployment process:

1. **Clone the repository** using `git`
2. **Install Python dependencies** using `uv`
3. **Install system dependencies** (nmap, dnsrecon, dnstwist, etc.)
4. **Configure the MCP server** for use

---

