n```bash\npip install uv\n```\n\nFor more information about installing uv, visit the [uv documentation](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/).\n\n## Integration with clients like Claude for Desktop\n\nOnce **uv** is installed, you can use the MCP server from any compatible client such as Claude for Desktop, in which case the steps to follow are:\n\n1. Go to **Claude > Settings > Developer > Edit Config > `claude_desktop_config.json`**\n2. Add the following block inside `\"mcpServers\"`:\n\n```json\n\"nasa-mcp\": {\n    \"command\": \"uvx\",\n    \"args\": [\n        \"nasa_mcp\"\n    ],\n    \"env\": {\n        \"NASA_API_KEY\": \"YOUR_NASA_API_KEY\"\n    }\n}\n```\n\n3. Get a free API key from NASA at: <https://api.nasa.gov/>\n4. Replace `YOUR_NASA_API_KEY` with your actual API key (leave the quotes). You can also use \"DEMO_KEY\" for limited testing.\n5. If you already have another MCP server configured, separate each with a comma `,`.\n\nIn general, to integrate it into any other MCP-compatible client such as Cursor, CODEGPT, or Roo Code, simply go to the MCP server configuration of your client and add the same code block.\n\n## Usage Examples\n\nOnce properly configured, you can ask things like:\n\n```\n- \"Show me today's astronomy picture of the day\"\n- \"Find asteroids that will pass near Earth in the next week\"\n- \"Get information about solar flares from January 2023\"\n- \"Show me Earth imagery for coordinates 29.78, -95.33\"\n- \"Find exoplanets in the habitable zone\"\n```\n","description_content_type":"text/markdown","docs_url":null,"download_url":null,"downloads":{"last_day":-1,"last_month":-1,"last_week":-1},"dynamic":["License-File"],"home_page":null,"keywords":null,"license":null,"license_expression":"MIT","license_files":["LICENSE"],"maintainer":null,"maintainer_email":null,"name":"nasa-mcp","package_url":"https://pypi.org/project/nasa-mcp/","platform":null,"project_url":"https://pypi.org/project/nasa-mcp/","project_urls":null,"provides_extra":null,"release_url":"https://pypi.org/project/nasa-mcp/0.1.0/","requires_dist":["httpx>=0.28.1","mcp[cli]>=1.6.0"],"requires_python":">=3.10","summary":"NASA API integration with MCP (Model Context Protocol)","version":"0.1.0","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},"last_serial":28799117,"ownership":{"organization":null,"roles":[{"role":"Owner","user":"ancode666"}]},"releases":{"0.1.0":[{"comment_text":null,"digests":{"blake2b_256":"e509baf9280252b94fbc9e400f7ec8de3613d0362b6c924a4063d94c71006529","md5":"7f081f302c576dff94a130af827dbc22","sha256":"a026ac15cd90d2e43b7bdc4146f5a6c2f4257a89b9cbabe7753ef770eefa72ed"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"nasa_mcp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"7f081f302c576dff94a130af827dbc22","packagetype":"bdist_wheel","python_version":"py3","requires_python":">=3.10","size":15469,"upload_time":"2025-04-30T06:27:58","upload_time_iso_8601":"2025-04-30T06:27:58.099124Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/e5/09/baf9280252b94fbc9e400f7ec8de3613d0362b6c924a4063d94c71006529/nasa_mcp-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},{"comment_text":null,"digests":{"blake2b_256":"324067db0587014c20ce87fae3e222404c89ae87b605d6d6dce7ab72a39056e7","md5":"389f7e88fbb297fd15b05653f31b60ca","sha256":"535f7b18367439a6a0cfac4125039fbea53b10878362824d823a01e0e88988df"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"nasa_mcp-0.1.0.tar.gz","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"389f7e88fbb297fd15b05653f31b60ca","packagetype":"sdist","python_version":"source","requires_python":">=3.10","size":16507,"upload_time":"2025-04-30T06:27:59","upload_time_iso_8601":"2025-04-30T06:27:59.202511Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/32/40/67db0587014c20ce87fae3e222404c89ae87b605d6d6dce7ab72a39056e7/nasa_mcp-0.1.0.tar.gz","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null}]},"urls":[{"comment_text":null,"digests":{"blake2b_256":"e509baf9280252b94fbc9e400f7ec8de3613d0362b6c924a4063d94c71006529","md5":"7f081f302c576dff94a130af827dbc22","sha256":"a026ac1